    metaTitle: 'Box Escape Par Score: Count Crate Pushes',
    metaDescription: 'Box Escape par score measures the fewest pushes needed to solve a level. Learn what counts, why walking is different and how to plan for a clean run.',
    imageTopic: 'box',
    tags: ['Box Escape par score', 'box pushing puzzle', 'crate push count', 'warehouse puzzle tips'],
    excerpt: 'Understand how par counts pushes rather than footsteps and plan crate moves without rushing for a perfect score.',
    secondaryKeywords: ['Box Escape pushes', 'fewest crate pushes', 'Box Escape stars', 'Sokoban par score', 'warehouse puzzle strategy'],
    longTailKeywords: ['what does par mean in Box Escape', 'does walking count toward par in Box Escape', 'how to get a perfect Box Escape score'],
    body: [
      'Box Escape par score is based on pushes, not every step your worker takes. Par records the fewest pushes needed to solve a level, so walking around a room to reach the correct side of a crate does not add to that push total. Matching par is a separate challenge from simply placing every crate on a target. Learn the safe solution first, then look for a shorter push sequence if you want the best score.',
      '@image:0',
      '## What counts as a push',
      '### Count crate movement, not footsteps',
      'A push happens when your worker moves into a crate and shifts it one square. A long route across empty floor is walking, while one contact that moves a box is a push. The difference matters because a path can be physically long and still use few pushes. Par lets the game compare the decisions that move the crates rather than the distance you travel between them.',
      'A single push can create several later options, so its value is not only the square the crate occupies next. You also need to stand on a useful side of the crate for the following move. In a tight room, walking around to change sides may take multiple steps. Those steps are necessary setup, even though par focuses on the crate movement.',
      '## Solve the room before minimizing it',
      'Start by asking which crate belongs on which target and what routes are available. Watch for corners and wall segments: a crate pushed into a non-target corner cannot be pulled back out. Also check narrow corridors where one crate can block another. A safe solution comes first because a low push count is no help if it traps a box before the final target is covered.',
      'Once you can finish without a deadlock, review the push sequence. Look for a move that sends a crate down a corridor earlier than necessary or pushes one box out of the way, then has to push it back. Sometimes a crate needs to move away from its target before it can reach the right approach side. That extra move may be essential, so do not remove it just because it looks like a detour.',
      '@image:1',
      '## Make a push plan around standing positions',
      'Before moving a crate, check whether you can reach the square behind it. The crate only moves away from your worker, so the side you occupy determines its direction. A target that appears open may still be unreachable if the room does not let you get behind the box. Trace a walking route to the required side before you push.',
      'After placing one crate, confirm that you have not blocked the route needed for another. When several crates share a hallway, the order can matter more than the number of steps. A crate temporarily parked against a wall might clear the center, but it can also close the only route around the room. Keep one or two future pushes in mind before committing.',
      '## Use the game’s par and hints carefully',
      'The level’s par gives you a reference for the shortest push solution. A hint shows the next push on a shortest solution, which can help when you are unsure about a crate’s destination. You do not need to use hints just to reach the targets. If you want to improve your push count, solve the level first and then compare your route with the hinted sequence.',
      'Undo takes back your last push, so use it when the crate ends up in a position that blocks a necessary route. Some traps are obvious, such as a non-target corner. Others become clear only when no remaining route lets a crate reach its target. If you are new to the rules, read the [Box Escape controls and rules](/blogs/box-escape-game-rules-and-controls) before comparing par.',
      '## Compare par with a safe route',
      'A shortest push solution can be harder to discover than a route with one extra move. If your first attempt clears the room without trapping a crate, you already know the level’s basic dependencies. On a replay, look for a single push that could be removed or combined with another. Do not change several crates at once, because it becomes difficult to tell which adjustment helped.',
      'Walking around a crate to reach its other side is sometimes essential even though walking does not count toward par. It may let you push a box away from a wall or line it up with a target. Treat the push count as a measure of crate decisions, not a demand to take the shortest walking path. A safe route that uses one extra push is a better foundation than a risky attempt at par.',
      '## Build a cleaner score one decision at a time',
      'Par is a useful target, but it does not mean every level should be solved in a hurry. Make a deliberate push, observe which floor squares remain reachable, and then choose the next crate. When a level is solved, use the result to see whether you matched the push target. If not, replay with one specific improvement in mind instead of changing every move.',
      'Try a room in [Box Escape](/play/box). First get every crate onto its target, then replay for fewer pushes. For a related crate puzzle with a broader set of layouts, see [how to solve Sokoban puzzles](/blogs/how-to-solve-sokoban-puzzles).',
    ],
    faq: [
      { q: 'What does par mean in Box Escape?', a: 'Par is the fewest pushes needed to solve the level.' },
      { q: 'Does walking count toward the Box Escape par?', a: 'No. Par counts crate pushes, not the steps you take across empty floor.' },
      { q: 'How does a hint help with par?', a: 'It shows the next push in a shortest solution, which can give you a route to compare with yours.' },
      { q: 'Should I chase par on my first attempt?', a: 'Learn a safe solution first. Then replay and look for unnecessary crate pushes.' },
    ],
